From: Erik Faye-Lund <erik.faye-lund@arm.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:08:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: track heap budget across instances

We used to track heap budget per heap inside each instance, but this
actually needs to be tracked across instances. There's a CTS test for
this now.

We take the same approach as RADV and ANV, of separating the heaps
from the budget and sharing a refcounted object across instances. This
unfortunately means we can't use vk_alloc et al for the allocations,
as those can't describe scopes larger than instance.

Fixes this CTS failure:
- dEQP-VK.info.device_memory_budget_multi_instance

Fixes: 65216acd8298 ("panvk: Implement VK_EXT_memory_budget support")
Reviewed-by: Aksel Hjerpbakk <aksel.hjerpbakk@arm.com>
(cherry picked from commit ba3dacb9832bd073198d22c402f4e0d75ec3a09a)

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45704>
(cherry picked from commit aaecf74c422)

